## The seven criteria

Evidence must cite **rows or facts**, not just a filename. "See requirements-register.md" is not evidence that acceptance criteria exist.

| # | Criterion | Status | Evidence | To close | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Named executive sponsor, aligned | | | | |
| 2 | Bounded scope with explicit non-goals | | | | |
| 3 | Defined value with a measured baseline | | | | |
| 4 | Feasible data | | | | |
| 5 | Known risks | | | | |
| 6 | Agreed acceptance criteria | | | | |
| 7 | Settled evidence-handling terms | | | | |

## Anti-pattern check

Confirm you checked your own draft for these before submitting it.

| Check | Confirmed |
|---|---|
| Not all green on first pass (on a real engagement this means it was written from intent, not evidence) | |
| "Partially met" used only with a stated remainder and an owner | |
| Criterion 4 checked twice — possible ≠ agreed ≠ provisioned | |
| Risk register contains something client-specific and uncomfortable | |
| Acceptance criteria have actually been seen by the client | |

